# [Sampling controls]($heading.id('sampling-and-speculative-decoding'))

The following [sampling controls](https://zml.ai/posts/llmd-20261112.0/#sampling-controls)
were documented for LLMD release `20261112.0`. Check your installed build for
the options it exposes.

| LLMD option | Default or fallback | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--top-k=<number>` | Unset, fallback `50` | Limit sampling to the highest-ranked tokens. |
| `--top-p=<fraction>` | Unset, fallback `1.0` | Keep tokens within a cumulative probability threshold. Accepted values are `0` through `1`. |
| `--min-p=<fraction>` | Unset, fallback `0.0` | Set a minimum probability threshold relative to the most probable token. Accepted values are `0` through `1`. |
| `--temperature=<number>` | Unset, fallback `1.0` | Scale the sampling distribution. |

For chat requests that support `temperature` or `top_p`, the request value
wins. The CLI value comes next, followed by the model's recommendation and
then the listed fallback. `top_k` and `min_p` start at the CLI level.

# [Speculative decoding flags]($heading.id('speculative-decoding-flags'))

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--speculative-drafter-model=<path>` | Unset | Enable speculative decoding with a compatible drafter checkpoint or `native` where supported. |
| `--speculative-draft-count=<tokens>` | Derived from the model configuration | Override the number of draft tokens to verify. |

# [Choose a decoding mode]($heading.id('choose-a-decoding-mode'))

Choose a checkpoint and decoding mode in [Model compatibility]($link.page('llmd/models')).
Run one server command at a time. These examples use LLMD's default batch
size, context length, and sampling settings.

**Standard decoding.** Pass only the target checkpoint.

```sh
llmd --model=hf://Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B
```

**Native multi-token prediction (MTP).** The target checkpoint supplies its
own drafter. Both `deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash` and
`Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next` have a routine native MTP configuration.

```sh
llmd --model=hf://Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next \
  --speculative-drafter-model=native
```

**External drafter.** Pass the exact drafter paired with the target checkpoint.
For Qwen3.8-27B, load the DFlash2 drafter from Hugging Face at launch.

```sh
llmd --model=hf://Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B \
  --speculative-drafter-model=hf://incoai/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2
```

For a local copy, use the quickstart's [checkpoint storage instructions]($link.page('llmd/quickstart').ref('checkpoint-storage'))
to download both repositories under `${HOME}/models`. A native installation
accepts the host directory for each.

```sh
llmd --model="${HOME}/models/Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B" \
  --speculative-drafter-model="${HOME}/models/incoai/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2"
```

On a CUDA Docker host, mount the two directories read-only and pass their
container paths to LLMD.

```sh
docker run --rm --gpus=all --shm-size=256GB -p 127.0.0.1:8000:8000 \
  --mount "type=bind,source=${HOME}/models/Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B,target=/model,readonly" \
  --mount "type=bind,source=${HOME}/models/incoai/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2,target=/drafter,readonly" \
  zmlai/llmd:cuda --model=/model --speculative-drafter-model=/drafter
```

Omit `--speculative-draft-count` to use the count derived from the model
configuration. To measure the effect, [compare decoding modes]($link.page('operations/benchmarking').ref('compare-decoding-modes')).
